exports[`coffeeshop/coffeeshop.squiffy 1`] = `
"export const story = {};
story.id = "00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000";
story.expressions = true;
story.panels = [
    {
        "passage": "order pad",
        "label": "Order pad",
        "position": "side"
    }
];
story.start = "intro";
story.sections = {
    "": {
        "text": "",
        "transition": "fade",
        "passages": {
            "order pad": {
                "text": "**Order pad**\\n\\n{{#each orders}}\\n- **{{@key}}:** {{this}}\\n{{else}}\\n_Nothing yet. Write down their orders._\\n{{/each}}\\n"
            }
        }
    },
    "intro": {
        "text": "The bell above the door jingles as you step into The Daily Grind for your first day of work.\\n\\nIt's a small independent coffee shop: mismatched armchairs, a specials board nobody has changed since spring, and a wall of local art with one empty hook in the middle of it. The air smells of espresso and burnt sugar.\\n\\nBehind the counter, the owner gives you a wave. \\"You must be the new hire! I'm Carla. Welcome aboard. Remind me of your name?\\"\\n\\n<input type=\\"text\\" data-attribute=\\"player_name\\" data-section=\\"Monday\\" placeholder=\\"Your name\\" required minlength=\\"2\\" maxlength=\\"30\\">\\n\\n{{section \\"Monday\\" text=\\"Tie on your apron\\"}}\\n",
        "attributes": [
            "warmth = { maya: 0, ellis: 0, sam: 0 }",
            "orders = {}"
        ]
    },
    "Monday": {
        "clear": true,
        "text": "## Monday, 7am\\n\\nCarla gives you the tour in four minutes flat: the till, the grinder, the cupboard where the oat milk hides, and the {{passage \\"espresso machine\\"}}.\\n\\n\\"Here's the secret,\\" she says, handing you a notepad. \\"Learn their names. Learn their orders. Get the order right before they ask, and they're yours for life.\\"\\n\\nThen she vanishes into the back office with a stack of invoices. \\"You'll be fine! The regulars are friendly. Mostly.\\"\\n\\nTwo of them are here already. In the corner booth, a woman in her late twenties glares at a laptop as if it owes her money. By the window, an older man in a pressed shirt stares into an empty cup.\\n\\nYou've got time to talk properly to one of them before the rush.\\n\\n{{section \\"Maya first\\" text=\\"The woman with the laptop\\"}}\\n\\n{{section \\"Ellis first\\" text=\\"The man by the window\\"}}\\n",
        "classes": [
            "morning"
        ],
        "passages": {
            "espresso machine": {
                "text": "You give it a friendly pat. It makes a noise like {{#style \\"shudder\\"}}a walrus in a tumble dryer{{/style}}.\\n\\n\\"That's normal!\\" Carla calls from the back.\\n"
            }
        }
    },
    "Maya first": {
        "text": "The woman looks up as you come over, startled, then grins.\\n\\n\\"Sorry, I didn't see you there. I'm Maya.\\" She turns the laptop round. The page says CHAPTER TWENTY-ONE, and nothing else. \\"Writer. Allegedly.\\"\\n\\n\\"{{player_name}}. First day. Can I get you anything?\\"\\n\\n\\"Oat milk latte, extra shot. And an ending, if you've got one going spare.\\" She laughs, but there's an edge to it. \\"Twenty chapters, and I still don't know what happens to her.\\"\\n\\nYou write _oat milk, extra shot_ on your pad, and underline it.\\n\\nBehind you, the man by the window lifts his cup. Carla gets to him before you can. \\"The usual, Ellis?\\" He nods.\\n\\n{{section \\"rush\\" text=\\"Here comes the rush\\"}}\\n",
        "attributes": [
            "warmth.maya+=1",
            "orders.Maya = \\"oat milk latte, extra shot\\""
        ]
    },
    "Ellis first": {
        "text": "The man looks up as you come over. He's in his seventies, neatly pressed, with the face of someone who has forgotten how to smile but remembers that he used to.\\n\\n\\"Morning. I'm {{player_name}}, I've just started...\\"\\n\\n\\"Ellis.\\" Not unkindly. \\"Coffee. Black. No room.\\"\\n\\nYou write it down. He watches you do it.\\n\\n\\"The girl who worked mornings before you used to say hello,\\" he says. \\"Every day. Every single day.\\" He looks back out of the window. \\"It was nice.\\"\\n\\nYou aren't sure what to say to that, so you say, \\"Hello, Ellis.\\" Something in his face moves, very slightly.\\n\\nIn the corner booth, the woman with the laptop waves an empty mug. Carla gets to her first. \\"Oat milk, extra shot, Maya?\\" \\"Carla, you're a saint.\\"\\n\\n{{section \\"rush\\" text=\\"Here comes the rush\\"}}\\n",
        "attributes": [
            "warmth.ellis+=1",
            "orders.Ellis = \\"black coffee, no room\\""
        ]
    },
    "rush": {
        "text": "At eight o'clock the door stops closing. Commuters, dog walkers, a man who orders a \\"small large\\" and won't explain. The espresso machine {{#style \\"shudder\\"}}groans{{/style}} like a ship in a storm.\\n\\nWhen it's over, both regulars have gone. {{#if warmth.maya}}Maya has left a napkin on the counter: _Thanks for asking. M._{{else}}Ellis has left exact change on his table, with one extra coin on top: the smallest possible tip. It feels like a medal.{{/if}}\\n\\nCarla sends you home at two. \\"Back at six. Evenings are different.\\"\\n\\n{{section \\"_continue1\\" text=\\"That evening...\\"}}"
    },
    "_continue1": {
        "clear": true,
        "text": "## Monday, 6pm\\n\\nAt night The Daily Grind turns into somewhere else. The big lights go off and the fairy lights come on, and the coffee crowd gives way to students, insomniacs, and a book group that hasn't talked about a book in years.\\n\\nIn the corner, someone in their early twenties sits alone: headphones round their neck, dark circles under their eyes, sketching in a battered notebook without looking at the page.\\n\\n{{section \\"Bring them a menu\\"}}\\n\\n{{section \\"Let them come to you\\"}}\\n",
        "classes": [
            "evening"
        ],
        "leave": "fade"
    },
    "Bring them a menu": {
        "text": "They jump when you put the menu down, then pull out an earbud.\\n\\n\\"Oh. Hi. Sorry.\\" They blink at the menu. \\"Whatever has the most caffeine? Like, medically inadvisable amounts.\\"\\n\\n\\"Long day?\\"\\n\\n\\"Long year.\\" It's almost a smile. \\"I'm Sam.\\"\\n\\n\\"{{player_name}}. First day.\\"\\n\\n\\"Welcome to the chaos.\\" Sam waves at the nearly empty room.\\n\\nOver their shoulder you can see the sketch: this room, in quick, sure lines. The counter. The fairy lights. The empty hook on the art wall.\\n\\n\\"That's really good.\\"\\n\\nSam snaps the notebook shut. \\"It's nothing. It keeps my hands busy.\\"\\n\\n{{section \\"Closing up\\"}}\\n",
        "attributes": [
            "warmth.sam+=1",
            "orders.Sam = \\"red-eye, as strong as it goes\\""
        ]
    },
    "Let them come to you": {
        "text": "Eventually they shuffle up to the counter, headphones still half on.\\n\\n\\"Red-eye. Please.\\"\\n\\n\\"Coming up. I'm {{player_name}}, by the way.\\"\\n\\n\\"Sam.\\" They pay in coins and go back to the corner, and pull the notebook close so that nobody can see what's in it.\\n\\n{{section \\"Closing up\\"}}\\n",
        "attributes": [
            "orders.Sam = \\"red-eye\\""
        ]
    },
    "Closing up": {
        "text": "Sam stays until closing, nursing one drink, filling page after page.\\n\\nAs you stack the chairs, Carla comes out of the back. \\"Good first day?\\"\\n\\n\\"Yeah. The regulars are...\\"\\n\\n\\"Interesting?\\"\\n\\n\\"I was going to say nice.\\"\\n\\nCarla smiles. \\"Give it time. They're both.\\"\\n\\n{{section \\"_continue2\\" text=\\"Tuesday\\"}}"
    },
    "_continue2": {
        "clear": true,
        "text": "## Tuesday, 7am\\n\\nEllis is in his seat by the window. Maya is in her booth, typing fast and deleting faster.\\n\\n{{#if orders.Ellis}}You don't need to ask what Ellis wants. You pour it before he's taken his coat off, and {{passage \\"Ellis on Tuesday\\" text=\\"take it over\\"}}.{{else}}You don't know what Ellis drinks. You could {{passage \\"Ellis on Tuesday\\" text=\\"ask him\\"}}.{{/if}}\\n\\nBefore you can do anything else, Maya beckons you over with the urgency of someone defusing a bomb.\\n\\n{{section \\"Maya on Tuesday\\" text=\\"See what Maya wants\\"}}\\n",
        "classes": [
            "morning"
        ],
        "leave": "fade",
        "passages": {
            "Ellis on Tuesday": {
                "text": "{{#if orders.Ellis}}\\n{{inc \\"warmth.ellis\\"}}\\nYou put the cup down in front of him. Black, no room. He looks at it, and then at you.\\n\\n\\"You remembered.\\"\\n\\nHe's quiet for a while. Then: \\"My wife and I came here every morning. Forty-three years. She had the hazelnut thing, with the cream on top. Too sweet. I told her every single day it was too sweet.\\" He turns the cup round on its saucer. \\"I'd give anything to buy her one more.\\"\\n\\nThere isn't anything to say to that. But you stay a moment, and that seems to be enough.\\n\\n\\"Thank you,\\" he says at last. \\"For listening.\\"\\n{{else}}\\n{{set \\"orders.Ellis\\" \\"black coffee, no room\\"}}\\n\\"Coffee,\\" he says. \\"Black. No room.\\" He says it slowly, the way you'd say something for the second time.\\n\\nYou write it down, and he watches you do it.\\n{{/if}}\\n"
            }
        }
    },
    "Maya on Tuesday": {
        "text": "{{#if warmth.maya}}\\"{{player_name}}! Thank goodness. I need a reader.\\"{{else}}\\"You're new. Good. Carla's sick of me. I need a reader.\\"{{/if}}\\n\\nShe spins the laptop round. \\"Last chapter. My heroine's on a station platform with a ticket out of this town in her hand. Everyone she loves is here. Everything she wants is out there. And I can't decide.\\" She pulls at her hair. \\"What would _you_ do?\\"\\n\\n{{section \\"Tuesday evening\\" text=\\"She gets on the train\\" set=\\" maya_idea = \\\\\\"train\\\\\\", warmth.maya += 1\\"}}\\n\\n{{section \\"Tuesday evening\\" text=\\"She stays\\" set=\\" maya_idea = \\\\\\"stays\\\\\\", warmth.maya += 1\\"}}\\n\\n{{section \\"Tuesday evening\\" text=\\"She misses it on purpose\\" set=\\" maya_idea = \\\\\\"misses\\\\\\", warmth.maya += 1\\"}}\\n"
    },
    "Tuesday evening": {
        "text": "Maya stares at you. Then she starts typing, and doesn't stop for three hours.\\n\\nThe afternoon blurs into the evening. The door opens and Sam shuffles in, looking exhausted, still in yesterday's clothes.\\n\\n{{#if warmth.sam}}\\"{{player_name}}.\\" A tired smile. \\"Please tell me you have coffee. And a will to live. I'll take either.\\"{{else}}\\"Red-eye.\\" They drop into the corner seat like a puppet with its strings cut.{{/if}}\\n\\n{{section \\"Check on Sam\\"}}\\n\\n{{section \\"Give them space\\"}}\\n",
        "classes": [
            "evening"
        ]
    },
    "Check on Sam": {
        "text": "You bring over a red-eye and sit across from them for a moment.\\n\\n\\"You okay?\\"\\n\\nSam blinks, as if the question doesn't compute.\\n\\n{{#if warmth.sam >= 2}}\\n\\"You asked me that yesterday too,\\" they say.\\n\\n\\"You looked like you needed it yesterday too.\\"\\n\\nSomething in their face shifts. They open the notebook and turn it round. It's the coffee shop again, but now there's someone behind the counter: you, drawn with real care.\\n\\n\\"There's an art school in the city,\\" Sam says, very quietly. \\"They want a portfolio by Friday. I've got forty drawings of this room, and I'm not sending any of them.\\" They close the notebook. \\"I don't show people. But you seem like you actually see people. You know?\\"\\n{{else}}\\n\\"Just tired,\\" they say. \\"It's nothing.\\"\\n\\nBut they don't put the headphones back on, and you take that as a good sign.\\n{{/if}}\\n\\n{{section \\"Tuesday night\\" text=\\"Close up for the night\\"}}\\n",
        "attributes": [
            "warmth.sam+=1"
        ]
    },
    "Give them space": {
        "text": "You leave the coffee and step away. Some people need room more than they need conversation.\\n\\nSam catches your eye as you go, and nods once. They understand.\\n\\n{{section \\"Tuesday night\\" text=\\"Close up for the night\\"}}\\n"
    },
    "Tuesday night": {
        "text": "You lock up, and walk home under the streetlights. Two days. That's all it's been. It feels like more.\\n\\n{{section \\"_continue3\\" text=\\"Wednesday\\"}}"
    },
    "_continue3": {
        "clear": true,
        "text": "## Wednesday, 7am\\n\\nCarla meets you at the door with a stick of chalk.\\n\\n\\"Tradition,\\" she says. \\"Every new barista names a drink for the specials board. Have a think. You've got until closing.\\"\\n\\nIt's your last day of training. Your regulars are all here, for once, at the same time.\\n\\n{{#if orders.Ellis}}{{passage \\"Ellis on Wednesday\\" text=\\"Ellis\\"}} is at the window.{{/if}} {{passage \\"Maya on Wednesday\\" text=\\"Maya\\"}} is in her booth, not typing, just reading. {{#if warmth.sam}}{{passage \\"Sam on Wednesday\\" text=\\"Sam\\"}}{{else}}Sam{{/if}} has come in early, which has never happened before.\\n\\nWhen you've done your rounds, it's {{section \\"closing time\\"}}.\\n",
        "classes": [
            "morning"
        ],
        "leave": "fade",
        "passages": {
            "Ellis on Wednesday": {
                "text": "{{#if warmth.ellis >= 2}}\\nHis coffee's on the table before he sits down. He nods his thanks, and then he looks at the counter, and you know what he's looking at: the bottle of hazelnut syrup.\\n\\nYou could {{passage \\"make the hazelnut thing\\"}}.\\n{{else}}\\n{{inc \\"warmth.ellis\\"}}\\nYou have his black coffee, no room, on the table before he's sat down.\\n\\nHe looks at it for a moment. \\"That's two of you,\\" he says. \\"Two who remembered.\\" He doesn't explain, but he says it like it matters.\\n{{/if}}\\n"
            },
            "make the hazelnut thing": {
                "text": "You make it carefully: the hazelnut, the cream on top, a dusting of cinnamon because it feels right. You set it down next to his coffee.\\n\\nHe stares at it for a long time. Long enough that you think you've made a terrible mistake.\\n\\nThen he picks it up, and takes a sip.\\n\\n\\"Too sweet,\\" he says. His eyes are wet. He's smiling. \\"She'd have liked you.\\"\\n",
                "attributes": [
                    "warmth.ellis+=1",
                    "made_hazelnut"
                ]
            },
            "Maya on Wednesday": {
                "text": "{{#if warmth.maya >= 2}}{{inc \\"warmth.maya\\"}}{{/if}}\\n\\"I finished it,\\" Maya says. \\"Three in the morning. I cried on the keyboard.\\" She turns the laptop round so you can read the last line:\\n\\n{{#if maya_idea = \\"train\\"}}\\n> _The train pulled out, and for the first time in her life she didn't look back._\\n{{else if maya_idea = \\"stays\\"}}\\n> _She tore the ticket in half, and walked back into town, and everyone she loved was still there._\\n{{else}}\\n> _She watched the train go without her, and realised she'd known all along that she would._\\n{{/if}}\\n\\n{{#if warmth.maya >= 3}}\\"There's a dedication, too,\\" she says, and goes pink. \\"_For the new barista, who asked._\\"{{else}}\\"It's good, isn't it?\\" She looks surprised. \\"It's actually good.\\"{{/if}}\\n"
            },
            "Sam on Wednesday": {
                "text": "{{#if warmth.sam >= 2}}\\nSam is drawing again. You look at the empty hook on the art wall, and then at them.\\n\\nYou could {{passage \\"ask about the hook\\"}}.\\n{{else}}\\nSam looks up from the notebook, and pulls out an earbud. \\"Morning, {{player_name}}.\\" It's the first time they've said your name.\\n{{/if}}\\n"
            },
            "ask about the hook": {
                "text": "\\"Carla,\\" you call. \\"That hook on the art wall. Is it free?\\"\\n\\n\\"Has been for a year,\\" Carla calls back. \\"Why?\\"\\n\\nSam has gone completely still. Then, slowly, they tear a page out of the notebook: the coffee shop, the fairy lights, and you behind the counter. They hold it out without looking at you.\\n\\n\\"If I can put one up here,\\" they say, \\"maybe I can send the others.\\"\\n",
                "attributes": [
                    "warmth.sam+=1",
                    "sam_on_the_wall"
                ]
            }
        }
    },
    "closing time": {
        "text": "The last customers drift out. Carla puts the chalk in your hand.\\n\\n\\"So? What's it called?\\"\\n\\n<input type=\\"text\\" data-attribute=\\"drink_name\\" data-section=\\"The specials board\\" placeholder=\\"Name your drink\\" required maxlength=\\"40\\">\\n\\n{{section \\"The specials board\\" text=\\"Write it on the board\\"}}\\n",
        "attributes": [
            "close_friends = (warmth.maya >= 2 ? 1 : 0) + (warmth.ellis >= 2 ? 1 : 0) + (warmth.sam >= 2 ? 1 : 0)"
        ]
    },
    "The specials board": {
        "clear": true,
        "text": "You write it in your best chalk capitals: **{{upper drink_name}}**.\\n\\n{{#if made_hazelnut}}It's hazelnut, with the cream on top. You both know it's too sweet.{{/if}}\\n\\n{{#if sam_on_the_wall}}On the art wall, the empty hook isn't empty any more.{{/if}}\\n\\n{{#if close_friends >= 2}}\\nCarla stands back and looks at the board for a long time.\\n\\n\\"Three days,\\" she says. \\"Most people take months. The regulars don't warm up to just anyone, you know.\\"\\n\\nShe hands you an apron: your own, with your name sewn on the front.\\n\\n\\"Welcome to The Daily Grind, {{player_name}}. You're one of us now.\\"\\n\\n**THE END: The New Regular**\\n{{else if close_friends = 1}}\\n\\"Not bad,\\" Carla says. \\"Not bad at all. Somebody in this shop is going to come in tomorrow hoping it's you behind the counter. That's how it starts.\\"\\n\\n\\"Same time tomorrow?\\"\\n\\n\\"Same time tomorrow.\\"\\n\\n**THE END: First Steps**\\n{{else}}\\nCarla studies you for a moment. \\"The regulars here have got their walls up. Most of us do. But this place has a way of bringing them down, if you give it time.\\"\\n\\nShe flips off the lights. \\"See you tomorrow?\\"\\n\\nYou nod. There's a lot still to learn about this place, and the people who call it home.\\n\\n**THE END: Room to Grow**\\n{{/if}}\\n\\n{{restart text=\\"Start your first week again\\"}}\\n",
        "leave": "fade"
    }
};
story.js = [
];"
`;

exports[`continue/continue.squiffy 1`] = `
"export const story = {};
story.id = "00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000";
story.start = "_default";
story.sections = {
    "_default": {
        "text": "Here is some text.\\n\\n{{section \\"_continue1\\" text=\\"Continue...\\"}}"
    },
    "_continue1": {
        "text": "More text.\\n\\n{{section \\"_continue2\\" text=\\"Carry on further...\\"}}"
    },
    "_continue2": {
        "text": "There's some more text now.\\n\\n{{section \\"_continue3\\" text=\\"Keep walking!\\"}}"
    },
    "_continue3": {
        "text": "Oh, even more text appeared!\\n\\n{{section \\"_continue4\\" text=\\"A little closer...\\"}}"
    },
    "_continue4": {
        "text": "Pretty scary.",
        "jsIndex": 0
    }
};
story.js = [
	(squiffy, get, set) => {
		alert("BOO!")
	},
];"
`;

exports[`gameshow/gameshow.squiffy 1`] = `
"export const story = {};
story.id = "00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000";
story.expressions = true;
story.panels = [
    {
        "passage": "scoreboard",
        "label": "Scoreboard",
        "position": "side"
    },
    {
        "passage": "prizes",
        "label": "Prizes",
        "icon": "star"
    },
    {
        "passage": "how to play",
        "label": "How to play",
        "icon": "help"
    }
];
story.settings = [
    {
        "name": "timers",
        "label": "Timed rounds",
        "description": "Turn this off to take as long as you like in Beat the Clock",
        "type": "toggle",
        "default": true
    },
    {
        "name": "lights",
        "label": "Studio lights",
        "type": "list",
        "options": [
            {
                "value": "Dazzling",
                "label": "Dazzling"
            },
            {
                "value": "Budget",
                "label": "Budget"
            }
        ],
        "default": "Dazzling"
    }
];
story.audio = [
    "sounds/theme.mp3",
    "sounds/applause.mp3",
    "sounds/ding.mp3",
    "sounds/fanfare.mp3",
    "sounds/buzzer.mp3"
];
story.start = "before the show";
story.sections = {
    "": {
        "text": "{{!--\\n    The Wheel of Dubious Fortune: a game show that shows off as much of Squiffy as it can.\\n\\n    This file has the start, the wheel, the commercial break, the final round and the endings.\\n    Each round is in a file of its own in rounds/, and squiffy.json adds the side panel, the\\n    Prizes and How to play buttons, and the player's settings. studio.css is the studio.\\n\\n    The theme tune, sounds/theme.mp3, is by Keehar.\\n--}}\\n{{!-- Push Hank too far, and the show's over, wherever you are --}}\\n{{#if patience <= 0 and not (at (array \\"Hank walks off\\" \\"Ending\\"))}}{{goto \\"Hank walks off\\" after=\\"1.5s\\"}}{{/if}}\\n",
        "transition": "fade",
        "passages": {
            "scoreboard": {
                "text": "{{#if player_name}}## {{player_name}}{{/if}}\\n\\n**Score:** {{score}}\\n\\n**Round:** {{#if round > 0}}{{round}} of {{rounds_tonight}}{{else}}Warm-up{{/if}}\\n\\n**Hank's patience:** {{#if patience > 0}}{{#each (range 1 patience)}}❤️{{/each}}{{else}}💔{{/if}}\\n_{{#if patience >= 3}}Cheerful{{else if patience = 2}}Strained{{else if patience = 1}}Brittle{{else}}Gone{{/if}}_\\n"
            },
            "prizes": {
                "text": "{{#each prizes}}\\n- {{this}}\\n{{else}}\\nYou haven't won anything yet. Hank says that's \\"very on brand for this show\\".\\n{{/each}}\\n"
            },
            "how to play": {
                "text": "Spin the wheel, play the round it lands on, and win as many points as you can. Three rounds, then the final question.\\n\\nBe nice to Hank. He's had a long day, and when his patience runs out, so does the show.\\n\\n**Studio lights** and **Timed rounds** are in the Settings. Turn off timed rounds to take as long as you like.\\n"
            }
        }
    },
    "before the show": {
        "text": "The studio is dark. A sign above the stage says ON AIR, but it isn't lit yet. Somewhere, someone is testing a microphone: \\"One, two. One, two. Is this thing... it is? Oh.\\"\\n\\n\\"Tonight's recording is about to begin,\\" says a voice. \\"Please switch off your phones, and laugh when the sign tells you to.\\"\\n\\n{{section \\"intro\\" text=\\"Take your seat\\"}}\\n",
        "attributes": [
            "score = 0",
            "round = 0",
            "patience = 3",
            "prizes = []",
            "rounds_tonight = 3",
            "wheel = [\\"General Knowledge\\", \\"Beat the Clock\\", \\"Professor Boom's Lab\\", \\"The Mystery Box\\", \\"The Audience Decides\\"]",
            "tonight = (slice (shuffle wheel) 0 rounds_tonight)"
        ]
    },
    "intro": {
        "text": "**{{#animate \\"typewriter\\" interval=120}}WELCOME TO...{{/animate}}**\\n\\n# {{#animate \\"toast\\" interval=250}}THE WHEEL OF {{#style \\"sway\\"}}DUBIOUS{{/style}} FORTUNE!{{/animate}}\\n\\n{{#animate \\"fadeIn\\" duration=1500}}\\nThe studio lights flicker. {{#if settings.lights = \\"Budget\\"}}Most of them stay off. Someone has taped a torch to a broom handle.{{else}}A thousand bulbs blaze into life, and three of them explode.{{/if}} A man in a sequined jacket stumbles onto the stage, holding his cue cards upside down.\\n\\n\\"Hello, and welcome! I'm your host, Chuck Wheelsworth!\\" He squints at the cards. \\"No, wait. I'm Hank Spinneroni. Definitely Hank.\\"\\n\\nThe studio audience (three people and a cardboard cutout) applauds uncertainly.\\n\\n\\"And YOU are tonight's lucky contestant! What's your name?\\"\\n\\n<input type=\\"text\\" data-attribute=\\"player_name\\" data-section=\\"contestant\\" placeholder=\\"Your name\\" required minlength=\\"2\\" maxlength=\\"24\\">\\n\\n{{section \\"contestant\\" text=\\"That's me!\\"}}\\n{{/animate}}\\n",
        "music": "sounds/theme.mp3"
    },
    "contestant": {
        "text": "{{#if (lower player_name) contains \\"hank\\"}}\\n\\"Another Hank!\\" Hank clutches his chest. \\"There can only be one, {{player_name}}. We'll settle this later. Possibly with swords.\\"\\n{{else if player_name.length > 12}}\\n\\"{{player_name}}! That's a lot of name. We'll need a bigger name badge.\\" A stagehand starts writing on a second badge.\\n{{else}}\\n\\"Welcome, {{player_name}}! Or as I like to call you... {{player_name}}!\\"\\n\\nHank waits for a laugh. None comes.\\n{{/if}}\\n\\n{{embed \\"motto\\"}}\\n\\n\\"Tonight, the wheel will choose your fate {{rounds_tonight}} times, from {{wheel.length}} exciting categories: {{join wheel \\", \\" \\" and \\"}}. Then it's the final question, for double or nothing! Now, {{#animate \\"continue\\" style=\\"wave\\"}}let's spin...{{/animate}}\\"\\n\\n{{#animate \\"typewriter\\"}}THE WHEEL OF DUBIOUS FORTUNE!{{/animate}}\\n\\n{{#animate \\"fadeIn\\"}}{{section \\"spin\\" text=\\"Spin the wheel!\\"}}{{/animate}}\\n",
        "music": null,
        "sounds": [
            "sounds/applause.mp3"
        ],
        "attributes": [
            "player_name = (capitalise player_name)"
        ]
    },
    "motto": {
        "text": "\\"Remember our motto: _{{random (array \\"Whose Fortune Is It Anyway? (Legally, Ours)\\" \\"Spin to Win! (Winning Not Guaranteed)\\" \\"It's Not Gambling If There's a Wheel\\")}}_\\"\\n"
    },
    "spin": {
        "text": "{{#if round = 1}}A rusty wheel descends from the ceiling on a fraying rope, wobbling dangerously.{{else}}The wheel creaks back down from the ceiling. It's wobbling more than before.{{/if}}\\n\\nHank gives it a mighty heave. It turns with a noise like a shopping trolley hitting a pothole:\\n\\n{{!-- Every 140ms, the wheel shows another category, until it lands. The links to the rounds are in\\n    a section of their own, embedded when it lands, so --check can see that every round is reachable --}}\\n{{#every 140}}{{inc \\"spins\\"}}{{#if spins >= 16}}{{stop}}{{sound \\"sounds/ding.mp3\\"}}{{#style \\"wheel\\"}}**{{upper landed}}!**{{/style}}\\n\\n{{embed \\"play the round\\"}}{{else}}{{#style \\"wheel\\"}}{{random wheel}}...{{/style}}{{/if}}{{/every}}\\n",
        "attributes": [
            "round+=1",
            "spins = 0",
            "landed = (first tonight)",
            "tonight = (slice tonight 1)"
        ]
    },
    "play the round": {
        "text": "{{#if landed = \\"General Knowledge\\"}}{{section \\"General Knowledge\\" text=\\"Let's play!\\"}}{{/if}}\\n{{#if landed = \\"Beat the Clock\\"}}{{section \\"Beat the Clock\\" text=\\"Let's play!\\"}}{{/if}}\\n{{#if landed = \\"Professor Boom's Lab\\"}}{{section \\"Professor Boom's Lab\\" text=\\"Let's play!\\"}}{{/if}}\\n{{#if landed = \\"The Mystery Box\\"}}{{section \\"The Mystery Box\\" text=\\"Let's play!\\"}}{{/if}}\\n{{#if landed = \\"The Audience Decides\\"}}{{section \\"The Audience Decides\\" text=\\"Let's play!\\"}}{{/if}}\\n"
    },
    "next round": {
        "text": "{{#if round = 1}}\\n\\"And we're off!\\" Hank checks his watch. \\"Wait. Is that the time? We'll be right back after these messages!\\"\\n\\n{{section \\"commercial break\\" text=\\"Cut to the adverts\\"}}\\n{{else if round < rounds_tonight}}\\nHank shuffles his cards. \\"Round {{= round + 1}}, {{player_name}}! Are you ready?\\"\\n\\n{{section \\"spin\\" text=\\"Spin the wheel!\\"}}\\n{{else}}\\nThe wheel retracts into the ceiling, shedding bolts.\\n\\n{{section \\"final question\\" text=\\"On to the final question\\"}}\\n{{/if}}\\n\\n{{!-- Commercials: the screen slides away to the left, and the advert slides in from the right --}}"
    },
    "commercial break": {
        "clear": true,
        "text": "{{#style \\"advert-card\\"}}\\n## Are YOUR wheels dubious?\\n\\nTry **SPINNERONI'S WHEEL WAX**, the wax that's {{#style \\"flicker\\"}}almost legal{{/style}} in {{random (array \\"seven\\" \\"eleven\\" \\"nearly four\\")}} countries!\\n\\n_\\"I use it on my wheel, and on my hair!\\"_ (Hank Spinneroni, paid spokesman)\\n\\nSide effects may include spinning, dizziness, and spontaneous game show appearances.\\n{{/style}}\\n\\nWhile the adverts run, you could {{saves text=\\"save your game\\"}}, or {{settings text=\\"adjust the studio lights\\"}}.\\n\\n{{section \\"_continue1\\" text=\\"Back to the show!\\"}}",
        "sounds": [
            "sounds/fanfare.mp3"
        ],
        "classes": [
            "advert"
        ],
        "transition": "slide-left",
        "leave": "slide-left"
    },
    "_continue1": {
        "clear": true,
        "text": "\\"And we're back! Round 2, {{player_name}}!\\"\\n\\n{{section \\"spin\\" text=\\"Spin the wheel!\\"}}\\n",
        "transition": "slide-left",
        "leave": "slide-left"
    },
    "final question": {
        "text": "The studio lights go red. {{#if settings.lights = \\"Budget\\"}}(Somebody has put a red sock over the torch.){{/if}} Dramatic music plays. Somebody backstage is humming it.\\n\\n{{#animate \\"typewriter\\"}}THE FINAL QUESTION{{/animate}}\\n\\n\\"This is it, {{player_name}}! You have **{{score}} points**, and this question is worth... {{#animate \\"toast\\"}}DOUBLE OR NOTHING!{{/animate}}\\"\\n\\nThe audience gasps. The cardboard cutout gasps too (the air conditioning came on).\\n\\n\\"Here's your final question:\\"\\n\\n{{#embed \\"cue card\\" points=\\"Double or nothing\\"}}**What is the name of your host?**{{/embed}}\\n\\n<input type=\\"text\\" data-attribute=\\"final_answer\\" data-section=\\"final answer\\" placeholder=\\"Your final answer\\" required>\\n\\n{{section \\"final answer\\" text=\\"That's my final answer\\"}}\\n",
        "music": "sounds/theme.mp3",
        "classes": [
            "final"
        ]
    },
    "final answer": {
        "text": "\\"{{final_answer}},\\" Hank repeats slowly. He leans in. The audience leans in. The cardboard cutout leans in, and has to be propped up again.\\n\\n\\"Is that your... final... answer?\\"\\n\\n{{section \\"the verdict\\" text=\\"It is\\"}}\\n",
        "music": null
    },
    "the verdict": {
        "text": "{{#if (lower final_answer) contains \\"hank\\"}}\\n{{sound \\"sounds/ding.mp3\\"}}\\n\\"CORRECT! I AM HANK SPINNERONI! Probably!\\"\\n\\n{{set \\"score\\" score * 2}}\\n{{#animate \\"toast\\"}}SCORE DOUBLED!{{/animate}}\\n{{else if (lower final_answer) contains \\"chuck\\"}}\\n{{sound \\"sounds/buzzer.mp3\\"}}\\n\\"That was my FIRST name! The WRONG first name! But you remembered SOMETHING!\\"\\n\\n{{inc \\"score\\" 50}}\\n\\"Fifty points, for listening at the start. That's more than my agent does.\\"\\n{{else}}\\n{{sound \\"sounds/buzzer.mp3\\"}}\\nHank stares at you. A vein throbs in his forehead.\\n\\n\\"It's HANK. My name is HANK. I said it at the START.\\"\\n\\n{{#if patience >= 2}}He takes a deep breath. \\"But you've been a delight, so I'm not taking your points away. That's the real double or nothing: I'm doing nothing.\\"{{else}}{{set \\"score\\" 0}}\\"Double or nothing, {{player_name}}. You get the nothing.\\"{{/if}}\\n{{/if}}\\n\\n{{section \\"Ending\\" text=\\"See how you did\\"}}\\n\\n{{!-- The endings --}}"
    },
    "Ending": {
        "clear": true,
        "text": "# Final score: {{#every 60}}{{set \\"counted\\" (min (counted + step) score)}}{{counted}}{{#if counted >= score}}{{stop}}{{/if}}{{/every}}\\n\\n{{#if score >= 600}}\\n{{sound \\"sounds/fanfare.mp3\\"}}\\n{{#animate \\"toast\\"}}GRAND CHAMPION!{{/animate}}\\n\\nBalloons fall from the ceiling. Confetti explodes. Professor Boom bursts out of the trapdoor to set off celebratory fireworks (indoors, against regulations).\\n\\nHank hands you an oversized novelty cheque. It bounces.\\n\\n\\"{{player_name}}, you're our GRAND CHAMPION! You've won fame, glory, and whatever prizes we can legally give you once the lawyers have watched the tape!\\"\\n\\nThe audience carries you out on their shoulders. The cardboard cutout leads the parade.\\n\\n**THE END: Grand Champion**\\n{{else if score >= 250}}\\n{{sound \\"sounds/applause.mp3\\"}}\\n{{#animate \\"toast\\"}}WINNER!{{/animate}}\\n\\n\\"That's... actually pretty good!\\" Hank shakes your hand, then checks it's still got all its rings.\\n\\nA stagehand gives you a gift basket: one (1) cheese, a voucher for 10% off at a shop that closed in 2019, and a sincere thank-you note from Hank.\\n\\n\\"Come back any time! Assuming we're not cancelled!\\"\\n\\n**THE END: Winner**\\n{{else}}\\nHank looks at his cards. He looks at you. He looks at the audience.\\n\\n\\"You know what? You showed up. You tried. And isn't that what really matters?\\"\\n\\n{{embed \\"motto\\"}}\\n\\n\\"No, actually, points are what matter. But good effort!\\"\\n\\nHe gives you a single balloon. It's already deflating.\\n\\n**THE END: Participant**\\n{{/if}}\\n\\n{{#if prizes.length}}You take home: {{join prizes \\", \\" \\" and \\"}}.{{/if}}\\n\\n{{restart text=\\"Play again\\"}}\\n",
        "music": "sounds/theme.mp3",
        "transition": "zoom",
        "transitionTime": 800,
        "leave": "zoom",
        "attributes": [
            "counted = 0",
            "step = (max 1 (floor (score / 15)))"
        ]
    },
    "Hank walks off": {
        "clear": true,
        "text": "Hank puts down his cue cards, very neatly, one on top of the other.\\n\\n\\"No,\\" he says. \\"No, I don't think so.\\"\\n\\nHe takes off the sequined jacket, folds it over his arm, and walks off the set. A door slams somewhere. A moment later the studio lights go out, {{#style \\"flicker\\"}}one by one{{/style}}.\\n\\nIn the dark, the cardboard cutout falls over.\\n\\n**THE END: Off Air**\\n\\nYou had {{score}} points. You'll never know what they were worth.\\n\\n{{restart text=\\"Try again, and be nicer to Hank\\"}}\\n\\n{{!-- Used by every round: the question, written on one of Hank's cue cards --}}",
        "music": null,
        "sounds": [
            "sounds/buzzer.mp3"
        ],
        "classes": [
            "lights-out"
        ],
        "transition": "fade",
        "transitionTime": 1000,
        "leave": "rumble"
    },
    "cue card": {
        "text": "{{#style \\"cue-card\\"}}\\n{{content}}\\n\\n_{{points}}_\\n{{/style}}\\n"
    },
    "The Audience Decides": {
        "text": "\\"THE AUDIENCE DECIDES!\\" Hank waves grandly at the audience. \\"Ladies and gentlemen and cardboard: what challenge should {{player_name}} face?\\"\\n\\n{{#each audience}}\\n- **{{name}}**, in {{seat}}, votes {{random (array \\"SING\\" \\"DANCE\\" \\"BLENDER\\") set=\\"vote\\"}}{{append \\"votes\\" vote}}{{#if @last}} (nobody knows how){{/if}}\\n{{/each}}\\n\\n{{#if (count votes \\"SING\\") >= 2}}{{set \\"challenge\\" \\"SING\\"}}{{else if (count votes \\"DANCE\\") >= 2}}{{set \\"challenge\\" \\"DANCE\\"}}{{else if (count votes \\"BLENDER\\") >= 2}}{{set \\"challenge\\" \\"BLENDER\\"}}{{else}}{{set \\"challenge\\" (first votes)}}\\"A tie! Doris has the casting vote!\\"{{/if}}\\n\\n{{#if challenge = \\"SING\\"}}\\n\\"You heard them! SING, {{player_name}}! Sing like your points depend on it! Because they do!\\"\\n\\n{{section \\"Sing beautifully\\"}}\\n\\n{{section \\"Sing terribly, on purpose\\"}}\\n{{else if challenge = \\"DANCE\\"}}\\n\\"DANCE! Show us your moves!\\"\\n\\n{{section \\"Dance like nobody's watching\\"}}\\n\\n{{section \\"Do the robot\\"}}\\n{{else}}\\n\\"An impression of a BLENDER! This is normal television!\\"\\n\\n{{section \\"WHIRRRRRR\\"}}\\n\\n{{section \\"Refuse, on grounds of dignity\\"}}\\n{{/if}}\\n",
        "attributes": [
            "audience = [{ name: \\"Doris\\", seat: \\"the front row\\" }, { name: \\"Gary\\", seat: \\"row C, asleep\\" }, { name: \\"Cardboard Steve\\", seat: \\"the aisle\\" }]",
            "votes = []"
        ]
    },
    "Sing beautifully": {
        "text": "You belt out an operatic version of the show's theme tune, making up the words as you go.\\n\\nThe audience is moved. Gary wakes up specially to applaud. 150 points!\\n\\n{{#animate \\"toast\\"}}STANDING OVATION!{{/animate}}\\n\\n{{section \\"next round\\" text=\\"Next round!\\"}}\\n",
        "sounds": [
            "sounds/applause.mp3"
        ],
        "attributes": [
            "score+=150"
        ]
    },
    "Sing terribly, on purpose": {
        "text": "You screech like a cat in a tumble dryer. On purpose. For art.\\n\\nHank: \\"That was... really something. Twenty-five points. Moving on. Quickly.\\"\\n\\n{{section \\"next round\\" text=\\"Next round!\\"}}\\n",
        "attributes": [
            "patience-=1",
            "score+=25"
        ]
    },
    "Dance like nobody's watching": {
        "text": "{{#style \\"sway\\"}}You dance like nobody's watching.{{/style}} Everybody is watching. There are cameras.\\n\\nCardboard Steve falls over, but approvingly. 125 points!\\n\\n{{section \\"next round\\" text=\\"Next round!\\"}}\\n",
        "sounds": [
            "sounds/applause.mp3"
        ],
        "attributes": [
            "score+=125"
        ]
    },
    "Do the robot": {
        "text": "You do the robot so convincingly that a stagehand tries to unplug you.\\n\\n{{#animate \\"toast\\"}}BEEP BOOP. 100 POINTS.{{/animate}}\\n\\n{{section \\"next round\\" text=\\"Next round!\\"}}\\n",
        "attributes": [
            "score+=100"
        ]
    },
    "WHIRRRRRR": {
        "text": "{{#style \\"shudder\\"}}You spin round, making blender noises.{{/style}} It's deeply unsettling. Doris asks if you do smoothies.\\n\\nProfessor Boom's voice echoes up from under the stage: \\"MAGNIFICENT!\\" 175 points!\\n\\n{{section \\"next round\\" text=\\"Next round!\\"}}\\n",
        "sounds": [
            "sounds/applause.mp3"
        ],
        "attributes": [
            "score+=175"
        ]
    },
    "Refuse, on grounds of dignity": {
        "text": "\\"I'm not doing that.\\"\\n\\nHank: \\"Fair enough. You keep your dignity, and your score stays exactly where it is.\\"\\n\\n{{section \\"next round\\" text=\\"Next round!\\"}}\\n",
        "attributes": [
            "patience-=1"
        ]
    },
    "Beat the Clock": {
        "text": "\\"It's time to... {{#animate \\"toast\\"}}BEAT THE CLOCK!{{/animate}}\\" Hank wheels out an enormous egg timer.\\n\\n{{#if settings.timers}}\\n\\"Name as many vegetables as you can! You've got {{clock}} seconds, and the clock starts with your first answer. Fifty points for each one!\\"\\n{{else}}\\n\\"Name as many vegetables as you can! Fifty points for each one!\\" He taps the egg timer. \\"Somebody's turned the clock off in the Settings, so take as long as you like.\\"\\n{{/if}}\\n\\n{{#label \\"clock\\"}}{{/label}}\\n\\nType a vegetable, and press Enter: <input type=\\"text\\" data-attribute=\\"guess\\" data-passage=\\"guess\\" placeholder=\\"A vegetable\\" maxlength=\\"30\\">\\n\\n{{section \\"time's up\\" text=\\"That's all I can think of\\"}}\\n",
        "sounds": [
            "sounds/fanfare.mp3"
        ],
        "attributes": [
            "found = []",
            "clock = 20",
            "clock_running = false",
            "vegetables = [\\"artichoke\\", \\"asparagus\\", \\"aubergine\\", \\"bean\\", \\"beetroot\\", \\"broccoli\\", \\"cabbage\\", \\"carrot\\", \\"cauliflower\\", \\"celery\\", \\"chard\\", \\"chickpea\\", \\"corn\\", \\"courgette\\", \\"cucumber\\", \\"eggplant\\", \\"fennel\\", \\"garlic\\", \\"kale\\", \\"leek\\", \\"lentil\\", \\"lettuce\\", \\"marrow\\", \\"mushroom\\", \\"okra\\", \\"onion\\", \\"parsnip\\", \\"pea\\", \\"pepper\\", \\"potato\\", \\"pumpkin\\", \\"radish\\", \\"rocket\\", \\"shallot\\", \\"spinach\\", \\"sprout\\", \\"squash\\", \\"swede\\", \\"sweet potato\\", \\"sweetcorn\\", \\"tomato\\", \\"turnip\\", \\"watercress\\", \\"yam\\", \\"zucchini\\"]"
        ],
        "passages": {
            "guess": {
                "repeat": true,
                "text": "{{set \\"word\\" (lower guess)}}\\n{{#if settings.timers and not clock_running}}{{set \\"clock_running\\" true}}{{#replace \\"clock\\"}}⏱️ {{#style \\"countdown\\"}}{{#every 1000}}{{dec \\"clock\\"}}{{#if clock <= 0}}{{stop}}{{goto \\"time's up\\"}}{{else}}{{clock}}{{/if}}{{/every}}{{/style}}{{/replace}}{{/if}}\\n{{#if not word}}\\nHank cups a hand to his ear. \\"I didn't catch that!\\"\\n{{else if found contains word}}\\n\\"You've said {{word}} already!\\"\\n{{else if vegetables contains word or vegetables contains (slice word 0 -1)}}\\n{{append \\"found\\" word}}{{sound \\"sounds/ding.mp3\\"}}✅ **{{capitalise word}}!**\\n{{else}}\\n{{sound \\"sounds/buzzer.mp3\\"}}❌ \\"{{guess}}? That's not a vegetable.\\"\\n{{/if}}\\n",
                "jsIndex": 0
            }
        }
    },
    "time's up": {
        "text": "{{#if found.length >= 5}}{{append \\"prizes\\" \\"a novelty marrow\\"}}{{/if}}\\n{{#if clock <= 0}}{{sound \\"sounds/buzzer.mp3\\"}}{{#animate \\"toast\\"}}TIME'S UP!{{/animate}}{{/if}}\\n\\n{{#if found.length = 0}}\\n{{dec \\"patience\\"}}\\n\\"Not ONE vegetable?\\" Hank is appalled. \\"Do you eat nothing but crisps, {{player_name}}?\\"\\n{{else}}\\n\\"You named {{found.length}}: {{join found \\", \\" \\" and \\"}}. That's {{= found.length * 50}} points!\\"\\n\\n{{#if found.length >= 5}}\\"And for five or more, you win our special prize: a novelty marrow!\\" It's a normal marrow, with googly eyes.{{/if}}\\n{{/if}}\\n\\n{{section \\"next round\\" text=\\"Next round!\\"}}\\n",
        "attributes": [
            "score += found.length * 50"
        ]
    },
    "General Knowledge": {
        "text": "\\"Ah, General Knowledge! The knowledge of generals! Or of... general... people.\\" Hank shuffles his cards, and drops two of them.\\n\\n{{#embed \\"cue card\\" points=\\"100 points\\"}}**What is the capital of France?**{{/embed}}\\n\\nYour answer: {{#label \\"answer\\"}}{{rotate (array \\"Paris\\" \\"London\\" \\"A baguette\\" \\"France doesn't exist\\") set=\\"gk_answer\\"}} _(click to change it)_{{/label}}\\n\\n{{#label \\"lock\\"}}{{passage \\"lock in\\" text=\\"Lock in your answer\\"}}{{/label}}\\n",
        "passages": {
            "lock in": {
                "text": "{{#replace \\"answer\\"}}**{{gk_answer}}**{{/replace}}\\n{{#replace \\"lock\\"}}**LOCKED IN!**{{/replace}}\\n{{#if gk_answer = \\"Paris\\"}}\\n{{sound \\"sounds/ding.mp3\\"}}{{inc \\"score\\" 100}}\\n{{#animate \\"toast\\"}}CORRECT!{{/animate}}\\n\\n\\"Paris! City of light, city of love, city of... bread?\\" Hank looks confused, but happy.\\n{{else if gk_answer = \\"A baguette\\"}}\\n{{sound \\"sounds/buzzer.mp3\\"}}{{dec \\"patience\\"}}{{append \\"prizes\\" \\"a slightly stale baguette\\"}}\\n\\"A baguette? A BAGUETTE?!\\" Hank's eye twitches. \\"That's not even a city, {{player_name}}!\\"\\n\\nA stagehand hands you a baguette anyway, for some reason. The cardboard cutout falls over.\\n{{else if gk_answer = \\"France doesn't exist\\"}}\\n{{sound \\"sounds/buzzer.mp3\\"}}{{dec \\"patience\\" 2}}\\nHank stares at you for a very long time.\\n\\n\\"Security? Please make a note that {{player_name}} is a flight risk.\\"\\n{{else}}\\n{{sound \\"sounds/buzzer.mp3\\"}}{{dec \\"patience\\"}}\\n\\"London? LONDON?!\\" Hank throws his cue cards in the air. \\"That's in a whole other country!\\"\\n{{/if}}\\n\\n{{section \\"next round\\" text=\\"Next round!\\"}}\\n"
            }
        }
    },
    "The Mystery Box": {
        "text": "A golden box descends from the ceiling on a frayed rope.\\n\\n{{#style \\"buoy\\"}}🎁{{/style}}\\n\\n\\"Ooh, the Mystery Box!\\" Hank claps his hands. \\"It could contain ANYTHING! A prize! A question! A live animal! We genuinely don't know: the intern who packed it quit this morning!\\"\\n\\nThe box rattles.\\n\\n{{section \\"open the box\\" text=\\"Open the box carefully\\"}}\\n\\n{{section \\"Shake the box first\\"}}\\n\\n{{section \\"Refuse to open it\\"}}\\n",
        "attributes": [
            "box = (random [\\"prize\\", \\"bees\\", \\"boxes\\", \\"philosophy\\", \\"goat\\"])"
        ]
    },
    "Shake the box first": {
        "text": "You shake the box. Something inside goes {{#if box = \\"bees\\"}}\\"BZZZZZZ\\", very crossly{{else if box = \\"goat\\"}}\\"CLANG\\", and then, quietly, \\"meh?\\"{{else if box = \\"boxes\\"}}\\"thud-thud-thud-thud\\"{{else}}\\"clink\\"{{/if}}.\\n\\n\\"Please don't shake the... you know what, fine. Open it.\\"\\n\\n{{section \\"open the box\\" text=\\"Open the box\\"}}\\n",
        "attributes": [
            "patience-=1"
        ]
    },
    "Refuse to open it": {
        "text": "\\"You HAVE to open it! It's the MYSTERY BOX! The mystery is legally required to be resolved!\\"\\n\\nHank is sweating now.\\n\\n{{section \\"open the box\\" text=\\"Fine, open the box\\"}}\\n",
        "attributes": [
            "patience-=2"
        ]
    },
    "open the box": {
        "text": "You lift the lid slowly...\\n\\n{{#if box = \\"prize\\"}}\\n{{sound \\"sounds/fanfare.mp3\\"}}{{inc \\"score\\" 300}}{{append \\"prizes\\" \\"a gold(ish) trophy\\"}}\\n{{#animate \\"toast\\"}}JACKPOT!{{/animate}}\\n\\nInside is a solid gold trophy in the shape of a wheel! It's been spray-painted, but still! 300 points!\\n{{else if box = \\"bees\\"}}\\n{{dec \\"patience\\"}}{{inc \\"score\\" 50}}{{append \\"prizes\\" \\"a bee called Kevin\\"}}\\n{{#animate \\"toast\\"}}BEES!{{/animate}}\\n\\nThe box is full of bees. They seem confused rather than angry.\\n\\n\\"Oh no, NOT AGAIN!\\" Hank runs in circles. \\"WHO KEEPS PUTTING BEES IN THE MYSTERY BOX?!\\"\\n\\nOne bee lands on your nose, considers its life choices, and decides to stay with you. You name him Kevin. Fifty points, for bravery.\\n{{else if box = \\"boxes\\"}}\\n{{inc \\"score\\" 100}}\\nInside the box is another, smaller box.\\n\\n{{#each (range 1 3)}}\\nInside {{#if @first}}that{{else}}THAT{{/if}} is an even smaller box.\\n{{/each}}\\n\\nInside the smallest box of all is a note: \\"{{player_name}} wins 100 points!\\"\\n\\n\\"The recursive box!\\" Hank nods wisely. \\"A classic.\\"\\n{{else if box = \\"philosophy\\"}}\\n{{inc \\"score\\" 75}}\\nInside is a small scroll. It reads:\\n\\n_\\"What IS a prize, really? Is not the true prize the friends we made along the way? Also, here are 75 points.\\"_\\n\\nHank wipes away a single tear. \\"Beautiful.\\"\\n{{else}}\\n{{inc \\"score\\" 150}}{{append \\"prizes\\" \\"a goat (on loan)\\"}}\\n{{#animate \\"toast\\"}}A GOAT!{{/animate}}\\n\\nThere's a goat in the box. You don't know how it fitted. Nor does the goat. 150 points, and the goat.\\n\\n\\"Is that... is that OUR goat?\\" says Hank. \\"Has it been in there since the Christmas special?\\"\\n{{/if}}\\n\\n{{section \\"next round\\" text=\\"Next round!\\"}}\\n"
    },
    "Professor Boom's Lab": {
        "text": "The lights flicker, and a trapdoor opens in the floor. Green smoke billows out.\\n\\n{{#animate \\"typewriter\\"}}PROFESSOR BOOM has entered the studio.{{/animate}}\\n\\nA wild-haired scientist climbs out, goggles askew, lab coat singed. \\"GREETINGS, QUIZ PARTICIPANT! Today you will invent a NEW ELEMENT!\\"\\n\\nHank backs away. \\"Professor, we talked about bringing chemicals on set...\\"\\n\\n\\"SILENCE, TELEVISION MAN!\\" The Professor waves at a shelf of bubbling flasks. \\"Mix me a compound! Seventy-five points for every ingredient! But mind the STABILITY!\\"\\n\\n**Lab stability:** {{live \\"lab.stability\\" passage=\\"stability\\"}}\\n\\n{{#each shelf}}\\n- {{passage \\"add\\" text=\\"Add the {{look}} one\\" set=\\" chemical = \\\\\\"{{name}}\\\\\\"\\"}}\\n{{/each}}\\n\\n{{section \\"compound\\" text=\\"Present your compound\\"}}\\n",
        "classes": [
            "lab"
        ],
        "transition": "rumble",
        "attributes": [
            "lab = { stability: 100, mixture: [] }",
            "shelf = [{ name: \\"Fizz\\", look: \\"fizzing blue\\" }, { name: \\"Sulk\\", look: \\"sulky green\\" }, { name: \\"Gloop\\", look: \\"suspiciously beige\\" }, { name: \\"Shriek\\", look: \\"screaming orange\\" }]"
        ],
        "passages": {
            "stability": {
                "text": "{{#if lab.stability <= 40}}{{#style \\"shake\\"}}**{{lab.stability}}%**{{/style}}{{else}}{{lab.stability}}%{{/if}}\\n"
            },
            "add": {
                "text": "{{append \\"lab.mixture\\" chemical}}{{set \\"lab.stability\\" lab.stability - (random (array 20 25 30 35))}}\\nYou pour in the {{lower chemical}}. The mixture turns {{random (array \\"a deep purple\\" \\"plaid\\" \\"the colour of a Tuesday\\" \\"transparent, which is worrying\\")}}.\\n\\n{{#if lab.stability <= 10}}\\n{{#style \\"rumble\\"}}The beaker starts to hum.{{/style}}{{goto \\"kaboom\\" after=\\"2s\\"}}\\n{{else if lab.stability <= 40}}\\nProfessor Boom: \\"HURRY! The compound is becoming... UNSTABLE!\\"\\n{{/if}}\\n"
            }
        }
    },
    "compound": {
        "text": "{{#if lab.mixture.length = 0}}\\n{{dec \\"patience\\"}}\\nYou hold up an empty beaker.\\n\\n\\"WATER?\\" Professor Boom's hair stands on end. \\"You've invented WATER?\\"\\n\\n\\"Technically it's just air,\\" says Hank.\\n\\n\\"GET OUT OF MY LABORATORY!\\"\\n{{else}}\\n{{sound \\"sounds/ding.mp3\\"}}{{append \\"prizes\\" (\\"a flask of \\" + element)}}\\nProfessor Boom holds your beaker up to the lights. Something in it blinks.\\n\\n\\"MAGNIFICENT! I shall call it... {{#animate \\"toast\\"}}{{upper element}}!{{/animate}}\\"\\n\\n\\"{{lab.mixture.length}} {{= lab.mixture.length = 1 ? \\"ingredient\\" : \\"ingredients\\"}}, {{= lab.mixture.length * 75}} points!\\" says Hank, from behind a fire extinguisher.\\n{{/if}}\\n\\nProfessor Boom vanishes back down the trapdoor, cackling. \\"UNTIL NEXT TIME! REMEMBER: SCIENCE IS JUST EXPLOSIONS IN A LAB COAT!\\"\\n\\n{{section \\"next round\\" text=\\"Next round!\\"}}\\n",
        "attributes": [
            "score += lab.mixture.length * 75",
            "element = (capitalise (lower (join lab.mixture \\"o\\"))) + \\"ium\\""
        ]
    },
    "kaboom": {
        "text": "{{#style \\"shake\\"}}**BOOM!**{{/style}}\\n\\nWhen the smoke clears, Hank has no eyebrows.\\n\\n\\"MY EYEBROWS!\\" he shrieks. \\"Those were RENTED!\\"\\n\\nProfessor Boom emerges from under a desk, delighted. \\"The finest explosion of the season! Twenty-five points, for SPECTACLE!\\"\\n\\n{{section \\"next round\\" text=\\"Next round!\\"}}\\n",
        "classes": [
            "lab"
        ],
        "transition": "rumble",
        "transitionTime": 1000,
        "attributes": [
            "patience-=1",
            "score += 25"
        ]
    }
};
story.js = [
	(squiffy, get, set) => {
		// Empties the text box, ready for the next guess
		squiffy.ui.afterWrite(() => {
		    const box = squiffy.element.querySelector("input[data-passage='guess']");
		    box.value = "";
		    box.focus();
		});
	},
];"
`;

